Classes can inherit from other classes, inheriting methods and attributes.
Methods inherited can retain their same functionality from the super/parent class and can also be modified to perform extra tasks.

Slicing:
list[3:5]
item at index 3 and 4. (Inclusive:Exclusive)
list[3:]
item at index 3 to the rest of the list
list[:3]
item at the start of the list to item at index 3 not inclusive
list[2:5:2]
every other item starting at 2
list[::2]
every other item in a list
list[::-1]
start from end of list to start